                {
                    "file": "/PATCHSET_LEVEL",
                    "line": 0,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Ed Tanous",
                        "email": "ed@tanous.net",
                        "username": "edtanous"
                    },
                    "message": "The default state file is the current directory, which is not changing in this patch.  What's the concern exactly?  yes, if you run from /home/root you'll have a conflict currently, but that's not something most do on a squashfs filesystem, right?  MOst run from temp and the state file will be created from temp?"
                },
